  "grammar_observation": {
    "target_language": "Fy mag i; dy fag di. Dy lyfr di; ei lyfr e; ei llyfr hi; ei hallwedd hi.",
    "bridge_language": "Welsh places fy, dy, or ei before the noun and often adds an echo pronoun after it. Fy causes nasal mutation (bag → mag); dy and masculine ei cause soft mutation (bag → fag, llyfr → lyfr); feminine ei causes aspirate mutation or h- before a vowel (allwedd → hallwedd)."
  },
